></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SASAKI, KATSUSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TEIJIN LIMITED</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUNAKOSHI WATARU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAGEYAMA YUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KANEKO HIROAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SASAKI KATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUNAKOSHI, WATARU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAGEYAMA, YUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANEKO, HIROAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SASAKI, KATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process for efficiently producing from a linear aromatic polycarbonate a high-quality thermoplastic branched polycarbonate for use in blow molding, extrusion, and vacuum forming. The thermoplastic branched polycarbonate is produced by melt-kneading a substantially linear aromatic polycarbonate together with an acid anhydride having at least two cyclic acid anhydride groups per molecule in the presence of a basic catalyst to thereby react them.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé efficace d'obtention d'un polycarbonate ramifié thermoplastique de qualité à partir d'un polycarbonate aromatique linéaire utilisé dans le moulage par soufflage, l'extrusion et le formage sous vide. Ce polycarbonate ramifié thermoplastique est obtenu par malaxage à chaud d'un polycarbonate aromatique linéaire avec un acide anhydre ayant au moins deux groupes d'acide anhydre cycliques par molécule destinés à réagir en présence d'un catalyseur basique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>